From 650b8aa1a6090bc83b6b3fea153ca38a04f4c5c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:13:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/42] media_server, bluetooth_audio: another output plays
 while the speakers are out of reach

An output can now tell the media server that it cannot play for now
(MEDIA_SERVER_SET_OUTPUT_AVAILABLE, with the node and true or false).
While the default audio output cannot, the rescan thread moves the mixer
to another output, marked as a stand-in as for a saved device that is
absent: the saved preference stays, and the existing return to the saved
default takes the sound back once it can play again. Outputs that cannot
play are no candidates for a default.

The Bluetooth audio node says so when there is sound to play and the
speakers do not answer, and calls them every 30 s meanwhile (the sound
goes elsewhere, so it no longer waits for them); it says they can play
again when it connects, or they do.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
